      "description": "Looking west across the northeast parcel of the CityCenterDC redevelopment project in Washington, D.C., in the United States in August 2011.  This portion of the project is owned by local developer Kingdon Gould III, and title to the lot was transferred to him on November 1, 2007, in exchange for a parcel of land he owned a few blocks to the north (on which the city intended lease to a developer for the construction of a large convention center hotel).  Gould remained undecided about what to construct on his parcel, and it remained in use as a surface parking lot as of August 2011 even as construction on the rest of the project began.",
